    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #327\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully.\n\n## Summary\n\nBranch: `bb/relay-121-agent-runtime-08-08-report-ai-utilizat-thr_52evi3pabp` (pushed to origin).\n\nImplemented the read-model core of issue #121: `getAiUsageReport()` in `backend/packages/data/src/aiGateway/aiUsageReport.ts`, aggregating `ai_gateway_calls` over a bounded, validated date range by provider, model, native unit (`tokens` vs `audio_seconds`), and the originating `agent_runs.unit` (`invocation`/`session`, or `null` for calls outside any run). It also returns a per-day cost series (bucketed in the system's configured timezone, matching the daily budget's own reset boundary) with explicit zeros for empty days, plus the current `AiBudgets` for cap/uncapped rendering. Nulls (no token/audio concept for a group) are never coerced to zero.\n\n**Scope note:** the issue also asks for an authenticated `GET /api/ai-usage` HTTP endpoint and a \"Semprec System page\" graph. This repo currently has no HTTP server, no auth middleware, and no charting library anywhere — `backend/services/` and `web/`'s page layer are explicit scaffolds, and the REST/auth transport is tracked as two separate, still-open epics (`generic-rest` #238-241, `auth-v1` #138-143). Every prior issue in this `agent-runtime` series stayed within `backend/packages/{data,agent-runtime}` for the same reason. I landed the aggregation logic at that same layer so it can be wired directly into a route once those epics land, rather than inventing throwaway server/auth/frontend infrastructure here.\n\n**Test results:**\n- Backend build: clean across all 10 packages.\n- Backend unit tests: 83/83 passed.\n- Backend integration tests: 489/490 passed — the 1 failure (`propertyTypeMigration.test.ts`, a concurrent-migration race test) is pre-existing and unrelated: it fails identically in isolation and touches none of the files this change modifies.\n- Backend e2e tests: 5/5 passed.\n- Dependency boundary check: no violations.\n- Web tests: 81/81 passed (untouched by this change).\n- New `aiUsageReport.test.ts` (5 tests): all passing.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
