    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #327\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed to branch `bb/relay-121-agent-runtime-08-08-report-ai-utilizat-thr_52evi3pabp`.\n\n## Summary\n\nThis addresses the code-review/CI feedback on PR #327 for issue #121 (\"[agent-runtime 08/08] Report AI utilization\").\n\n**Fixed the medium-severity finding:** `run_unit` in `aiUsageReport.ts` is now validated via `assertKnownValue()` before being widened to `AgentRunUnit | null`, per the project's DB-row-validation convention.\n\n**Delivered the previously-missing scope** the review bot flagged as blocking:\n\n- `backend/services/semprec-api`: a new service package exposing authenticated `GET /api/ai-usage`. It's a testable request-handler function (`createAiUsageRequestListener`) rather than a running process — the caller owns the actual HTTP server, matching the existing `@semprec/realtime` wiring pattern. Auth is a stopgap bearer-token check via an explicit parameter (never hardcoded/logged), meant to be swapped out once the `auth-v1` epic lands. `ChokePointError` subclasses map to their HTTP status; unexpected errors return 500. Tested with real HTTP requests against the real ephemeral integration Postgres.\n- `web/src/views/aiUsage/UtilizationPage.tsx`: the System page's Utilization graph — an inline-SVG cost-per-day chart with an explicit daily-budget reference line, days over budget highlighted, explicit \"uncapped\" text when the monthly budget is null, and a breakdown table that represents audio-only calls by their own unit instead of showing 0 tokens. Built on the existing `StateViews` (loading/empty/error), `useTranslate()`, and the `OperationError`/`OperationFailureKind` pattern, with new strings added to both `en` and `cs` catalogs. Routed via a new `?page=ai-usage` composition-root entry (not a choke-point item/view, so it doesn't reuse `?view=`).\n\n**Verification:** backend unit (83/83), integration (495/495 — one known pre-existing/flaky concurrency test reconfirmed unrelated and stable in isolation), and e2e (5/5) suites pass; `check:boundaries` passes; both backend and web typecheck cleanly; web test suite (86/86) passes, including new tests for both the HTTP handler and the Utilization page.\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
